      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5acad9ecc9dba010c9c3ec68|full_name}: Thanks for the response! I support any solution that allows us to show an individual avatar without having to always override safety settings. Go with whatever idea makes the most sense and is easier to implement.\nThis feature would be extremely useful because then we wouldn't have to download/show 25+ avatars if we could just manually toggle on a few at a time. The game would run way smoother and it doesn't really make sense to download people we aren't gonna talk to anyway. It's just wasted resources in my opinion.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-03-19T04:08:56.144Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "It would be nice to keep most avatars turned off but also have an option to manually toggle on avatars for specific individuals WITHOUT seeing their shaders, particles, animations, ect... (like custom safety settings)\n\nThe only option we have right now is the \"show avatar\" button and it overrides the safety settings which isn't ideal in public worlds because of crashers/performance loss.\n\nThis would also be a simple way to increase performance & minimize bandwidth for a lot of players! (if they choose to play like this)",
